So now that you know everything there is to know about routing, let's take a look at how we can actually fetch data within those routes.

506
00:48:08,014 --> 00:48:16,004
在传统的 React 应用中，你可能会在 use_effect 钩子中写一个标准的 fetch 请求。
Inside of a traditional React application, you would probably write a standard fetch request inside of a use effect hook.

507
00:48:16,590 --> 00:48:24,452
组件挂载，钩子触发，用户就在那里盯着旋转的加载圈，等待网络连接。
The component mounts, the hook fires, and the user stares at a spinning loading wheel while they wait for the network to connect.

508
00:48:25,070 --> 00:48:28,004
我们称之为渲染获取瀑布流。
We call this the render fetch waterfall.

509
00:48:28,494 --> 00:48:38,404
浏览器必须下载 JavaScript、解析它、启动 React、渲染布局，然后它才意识到需要去抓取数据。
The browser has to download JavaScript, parse it, boot up React, render the layout, and only then does it realize it needs to grab data.

510
00:48:38,990 --> 00:48:45,700
TanStack Start 利用被称为路由加载器的东西，完全解决了这个问题。
Canstack start completely eliminates this problem using something known as route loaders.

511
00:48:46,030 --> 00:48:51,908
加载器是一个直接关联到你的路由文件中的专用异步函数。
A loader is a dedicated asynchronous function attached directly to your route file.

512
00:48:52,462 --> 00:48:58,084
当用户点击链接访问新页面时，路由器会拦截该点击操作。
When a user clicks a link to visit a new page, the router intercepts that click.

513
00:48:58,414 --> 00:49:05,092
因此，在 React 尝试渲染下一个组件之前，路由器就会触发加载器来获取数据。
So before React even attempts to render the next component, the router fires the loader to grab the data.

514
00:49:05,614 --> 00:49:11,076
这样到组件真正渲染时，数据就已经在那儿等着了。
So by the time the component actually renders, the data is already sitting there waiting.

515
00:49:11,502 --> 00:49:15,748
所以用户能获得瞬时的跳转，且没有任何布局偏移。
So the user gets an instant transition with zero layout shift.

